/-!
# Component selection in the A₅ centralizer argument

This development fixes the literal star and plus action quotients, their
subgroup families and maps. It proves 13.6.12 by propagating centralization
from z to U_v, and proves that Y_z membership transfers between local
components with the same star image. The star-to-plus map is surjective,
with its exact kernel and compatible action proved.

The geometric and Thompson reductions, FF-module exclusions, existence
of a member of Y_z, and the component/module conclusions of 13.6.14–16
remain to be proved and assembled. In particular, no selected-component
or centralizer-containment theorem is asserted by these partial results.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, The Classification of Quasithin Groups, combined
1 March 2004 manuscript, printed pp.928–930.
-/
